                    ${row.viewerWebUsd.toFixed(2)}
                  </td>
                  <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-right text-muted font-mono tabular-nums">
                    ${row.twitchCutUsd.toFixed(2)}
                  </td>
                  <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-right font-semibold text-ink font-mono tabular-nums">
                    {row.creatorSharePct.toFixed(1)}%
                  </td>
                  <td class="py-3.5 px-4 text-caption text-muted">
                    {row.discountBadge ? (
                      <span class="inline-block px-2 py-0.5 rounded-xxs bg-mint-50 border border-mint-200 text-primary font-semibold text-micro">
                        {row.discountBadge}
                      </span>
                    ) : (
                      "Standard $0.014/bit rate"
                    )}
                  </td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
            <tfoot class="bg-canvas-soft border-t-2 border-hairline-strong font-bold text-caption text-muted">
              <tr>
                <td colspan="6" class="py-3 px-4">
                  * Note: Mobile app purchases (iOS App Store & Google Play)
                  cost approximately 30% more due to mobile platform store fees
                  (e.g. $1.99 for 100 bits). Streamer payout remains fixed at
                  $0.01 USD per bit.
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tfoot>
          </table>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 5. How Twitch Bits Economics Work (No Filler) -->
    <section class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-heading-2 font-bold text-ink">
          How Twitch Bits Economics Work
        </h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-muted max-w-2xl">
          Unlike subscriptions which take a 50/50 revenue split on payout, Bits
          revenue is paid out in full to the creator.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas space-y-2">
          <span class="text-ui-label font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block">
            1. Streamer Keeps 100%
          </span>
          <p class="text-heading-4 font-mono font-bold text-ink">
            $0.01 per Bit Flat
          </p>
          <p class="text-caption text-muted">
            Whether a viewer cheers 1 bit or 100,000 bits, you receive exactly
            one penny per bit with no backend Twitch cut.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas space-y-2">
          <span class="text-ui-label font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block">
            2. Upfront Markup
          </span>
          <p class="text-heading-4 font-mono font-bold text-ink">
            ~28% to 40% Viewer Markup
          </p>
          <p class="text-caption text-muted">
            Twitch charges the viewer a markup when buying the bundle to cover
            credit card processing, infrastructure, and margin.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p-5 rounded-lg border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas space-y-2">
          <span class="text-ui-label font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block">
            3. $50 Payout Threshold
          </span>
          <p class="text-heading-4 font-mono font-bold text-ink">
            5,000 Bits Minimum
          </p>
          <p class="text-caption text-muted">
            Bits pool together with subscription revenue and ad earnings toward
            the standard $50 threshold for monthly payouts.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 6. FAQ Section -->
    <section class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-heading-2 font-bold text-ink">
          Frequently Asked Questions About Twitch Bits
        </h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-muted max-w-2xl">
          Common questions on cheering conversions, payout schedules, and bank
          transfer fees.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="group rounded-lg border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas p-4 transition-colors hover:border-primary">
            <summary class="flex items-center justify-between min-h-[44px] py-1 font-bold text-ink text-ui-label cursor-pointer list-none select-none">
              <span>{faq.question}</span>
              <svg
                class="w-4 h-4 text-muted group-open:rotate-180 transition-transform duration-150 shrink-0 ml-2"
                width="16"
                height="16"
                viewBox="0 0 20 20"
                fill="currentColor"
                aria-hidden="true"
              >
                <path
                  fill-rule="evenodd"
                  d="M5.23 7.21a.75.75 0 011.06.02L10 11.168l3.71-3.938a.75.75 0 111.08 1.04l-4.25 4.5a.75.75 0 01-1.08 0l-4.25-4.5a.75.75 0 01.02-1.06z"
                  clip-rule="evenodd"
                />
              </svg>
            </summary>
            <div class="mt-3 text-body text-body-sm leading-relaxed border-t border-hairline pt-3">
              {faq.answer}
            </div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 7. Related Calculators Grid -->
    <section class="space-y-6 pt-6 border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="space-y-2">
        <h2 class="text-heading-2 font-bold text-ink">
          More Creator & Seller Fee Calculators
        </h2>
        <p class="text-body-md text-muted max-w-2xl">
          Monetizing across multiple live or e-commerce platforms? Calculate
          your exact net payout.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
        {[
          {
            name: "Whatnot Fee Calculator",
            rate: "8.0% + 2.9% + $0.30",
            desc: "Calculate live auction fees, card processing, and net payouts for livestream sellers.",
            href: "/whatnot-fee-calculator/",
          },
          {
            name: "TikTok Shop Fee Calculator",
            rate: "6.0% + $0.30",
            desc: "Calculate live-shopping referral fees, affiliate creator commissions, and margins.",
            href: "/tiktok-shop-fee-calculator/",
          },
          {
            name: "Etsy Fee Calculator",
            rate: "6.5% + $0.20 + 3% + $0.25",
            desc: "Calculate handmade marketplace fees, listing fees, and processing costs.",
            href: "/etsy-fee-calculator/",
          },
          {
            name: "Depop Fee Calculator",
            rate: "0% selling + 3.3% + $0.45",
            desc: "Calculate marketplace processing fees for vintage apparel and second-hand fashion.",
            href: "/depop-fee-calculator/",
          },
          {
            name: "eBay US Fee Calculator",
            rate: "13.25% + $0.40",
            desc: "Calculate final value fees, store subscription discounts, and promoted listing rates.",
            href: "/ebay-fee-calculator/",
          },
          {
            name: "Etsy Offsite Ads Calculator",
            rate: "15% / 12% ($100 cap)",
            desc: "Model the impact of Etsy external advertising deductions on your net margins.",
            href: "/etsy-offsite-ads-fee-calculator/",
          },
        ].map((item) => (
          <a
            href={item.href}
            class="block rounded-lg border border-hairline-strong bg-canvas p-5 hover:border-primary hover:bg-mint-50/40 transition-colors focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary shadow-sm"
          >
            <span class="text-caption font-bold text-primary block mb-1">
              {item.rate}
            </span>
            <span class="text-heading-4 font-bold text-ink block mb-2">
              {item.name}
            </span>
            <span class="text-caption text-muted block">{item.desc}</span>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 8. Last-Verified Stamp -->
    <footer class="pt-6 border-t border-hairline">
      <div class="rounded-lg border border-mint-200 bg-mint-50 dark:bg-mint-200/10 p-5 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-4">
        <div class="space-y-1">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span
              class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-primary shrink-0"
              aria-hidden="true"
            ></span>
            <span class="text-ui-label font-bold text-ink">
              Official Rate Verification
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-caption text-muted">
            Twitch Bits terms and payout schedule officially verified on{" "}
            <strong class="text-ink">{verifiedDateFormatted}</strong>. Sourced
            directly from Twitch’s Guide to Cheering with Bits.
          </p>
        </div>

        <a
          href={sourceUrl}
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-4 py-2.5 min-h-[44px] bg-canvas border border-hairline-strong hover:border-primary rounded-xs text-ui-sm font-bold text-primary transition-colors shrink-0 focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-primary"
        >
